ne wording correction: the requirement to ignore\n       unrecognised members applies to readers; -00 said \"index\".\n    \n    Acknowledgements\n    \n       Thanks to the authors of [I-D.jimenez-dawn-discovery-landscape].\n    \n    Author's Address\n    \n       Aleksandr Artamokhov\n       Independent\n       Email: alexar76@rambler.ru--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndraft-artamokhov-dawn-marketplace-discovery-02 (https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/draft-artamokhov-dawn-marketplace-discovery-02)\nciteturn18search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: last week; Crawled: last week; draft-artamokhov-dawn-marketplace-discovery-02 Internet-Draft ...     \"AIMarket Protocol v2 test vectors and conformance runner\", 2026, <https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-protocol/tree/main/test-vectors>.\n\ndraft-artamokhov-dawn-marketplace-discovery-02 Internet-Draft\n\n | Title  |  | A Discovery Document and Signed Catalogue for Capability Marketplaces\nDocument  | Document type  |  | This is an older version of an Internet-Draft whose latest revision state is \"Active\". This document is an Internet-Draft (I-D). Anyone may submit an I-D to the IETF. This I-D is not endorsed by the IETF and has no formal standing in the IETF standards process.\n\nInternet-Draft  | Marketplace Discovery  | November 2026\nArtamokhov  | Expires 6 May 2027  | [Page]\n\nWorkgroup:\n    Network Working Group\nInternet-Draft:\n    draft-artamokhov-dawn-marketplace-discovery-02\nPublished:\n    2 November 2026\nIntended Status:\n    Standards Track\nExpires:\n    6 May 2027\nAuthor:\n    \n\nA. Artamokhov\n\nIndependent\n\n# A Discovery Document and Signed Catalogue for Capability Marketplaces\n\n## Abstract\n\nThis document defines a JSON discovery document, served at a well-known URI, that carries the public properties a client needs before using a capability index: its name, the protocol versions it serves, the location of its catalogue, and the key that signs the catalogue. ## 8. Implementation Status\n\nThis section records the status of known implementations at the time of writing, per [RFC7942]. It is to be removed before publication as an RFC.¶\n\n  * Reference implementation (Apache-2.0), deployed on six public indexes operated by the author or affiliated parties. Since 2026-10-30 they serve this document at `/.well-known/agent-marketplace` in addition to the earlier path `/.well-known/ai-market.json`, which uses the member names in Appendix \"Mapping to the deployed wire format\".¶\n\n  * Three further implementations by the same author, written from the text and test vectors without the reference source: a Go directory node, a Rust catalogue verifier, and a JavaScript verifier. Writing them found four ambiguities in the text, which were corrected.¶\n\n  * Two services operated by parties unrelated to the author publish catalogues that verify under `ed25519-pipe-2` (checked on 2026-10-30 with the conformance runner in [VECTORS]). --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA Discovery Document and Signed Catalogue for Capability Marketplaces (https://www.ietf.org/archive/id/draft-artamokhov-dawn-marketplace-discovery-00.html)\nciteturn18search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: last week; Crawled: last week; Aleksandr Artamokhov ... Email: alexar76@rambler.ru\n\n## Mapping to the authors' current wire format\n\nFor readers of the authors' deployed protocol, the correspondence is:¶\n\nTable 2\nThis document  | Deployed format\n--- | ---\n`/.well-known/agent-marketplace`  | `/.well-known/ai-market.json`\n`catalogue_url`  | `manifest_url`\n`capabilities`  | `tools`\n`signature_profile`  | implied; always `ed25519-pipe-2`\n`peers` (array of URI)  | `peers` (array of object with `url`)\n\nThe canonical string, digest rule and verification rule are identical, so a signature valid under one is valid under the other.¶\n\n## Acknowledgements\n\nEvery normative rule in Section 5 exists because its absence caused a concrete failure in a deployed system: a missing digest that let one implementation federate nothing, a vector set that signed too little, a bare-string signature that crashed three verifiers, and a permissive Ed25519 library that accepted a forgeable key. The authors thank the authors of [I-D.jimenez-dawn-discovery-landscape] for a survey that made the shape of the gap visible.¶\n\n## Author's Address\n\nAleksandr Artamokhov\n\nIndependent\n\nEmail: alexar76@rambler.ru--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nIndex of /pub/files/index/doc/netinfo/internet-drafts (https://mirrors.nic.funet.fi/pub/files/index/doc/netinfo/internet-drafts/)\nciteturn18search10 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week;     Image: [TXT] draft-artamokhov-dawn-index-federation-01.html              2026-10-30 10:47   87K  Federation Between Capability Indexes: Crawl, Reciprocal Identification and Admission\n    Image: [TXT] draft-artamokhov-dawn-index-federation-01.txt               2026-10-30 10:47   26K  \n    Image: [   ] draft-artamokhov-dawn-index-federation-01.xml               2026-10-30 10:47   43K  \n    Image: [TXT] draft-artamokhov-dawn-marketplace-discovery-02.html         2026-11-02 13:05  104K  A Discovery Document and Signed Catalogue for Capability Marketplaces\n    Image: [TXT] draft-artamokhov-dawn-marketplace-discovery-02.txt          2026-11-02 13:05   34K  \n    Image: [   ] draft-artamokhov-dawn-marketplace-discovery-02.xml          2026-11-02 13:05   53K  \n    Image: [TXT] draft-asor-wimse-agent-delegation-chain-03.html             2026-10-27 17:08  186K  Verifiable Attenuated Delegation for AI Agent Chains\n    Image: [TXT] draft-asor-wimse-agent-delegation-chain-03.txt              2026-10-27 17:08  102K  \n    Image: [   ] draft-asor-wimse-agent-delegation-chain-03.xml              2026-10-27 17:08  165K  \n    Image: [TXT] draft-asw-lsr-isis-ogid-00.html                             2026-11-02 09:18 